# Docker build context for the coordinator image, which is built from the repo root:
#   docker build -f agentic-orchestration-tool/docker/Dockerfile.coordinator .
#
# Without this file the whole checkout — .git, node_modules, local .env files,
# runtime state with API tokens and session history — is sent to the Docker daemon,
# and `COPY agentic-orchestration-tool/config` bakes per-host files into the image.
# (The worker image builds from agentic-orchestration-tool/ and has its own
# .dockerignore there.)

.git
.github
.cursor
.githooks

# Dependencies and caches
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/out-tsc

# Secrets and per-host configuration — never in an image
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/.secrets
agentic-orchestration-tool/config/env.host

# Runtime state (sessions, KB, learning, run traces, LLM usage, API tokens, mTLS CA, deals)
**/__orchestrator_*
**/__output__
**/_web_uploads
**/_tool_artifacts
**/_tool_sandbox
**/harness_runs
var
agentic-orchestration-web/public/admin/deploy-stamp.json

# Not part of the coordinator image
agentic-orchestration-admin
agentic-orchestration-tool/tests
agentic-orchestration-tool/scripts
agentic-orchestration-tool/deploy
agentic-orchestration-tool/docker
agentic-orchestration-tool/.tools
agentic-orchestration-tool/.mirrord
agentic-orchestration-web/test
docs
site
examples
extras
assets
*.png
*.md
